"panel\">\n      <div class=\"hd\">Fire Status Key</div>\n      <div class=\"bd\">\n       <div class=\"kv\"><span>Ready to shoot</span><b>RDY</b></div>\n       <div class=\"kv\"><span>Rocket launched</span><b>LNCH</b></div>\n       <div class=\"kv\"><span>Intercepted</span><b>INT</b></div>\n       <div class=\"kv\"><span>Miss</span><b>MISS</b></div>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n\n   </div>\n\n   <div class=\"footer\">\n    <div class=\"panel decision\">\n     <div class=\"hd\">Engagement Control <span class=\"r\">limit: two rockets in the air</span></div>\n     <div class=\"bd\">\n      <div class=\"seqhint\"><u>1 select track</u><u>2 target type</u><u>3 classification</u><u>4 interceptor</u><u>5 launcher</u><u>6 review tti / pk</u><u>7 fire / cease fire</u><u>radar tilt</u></div>\n      <div data-slot=\"decision\"></div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"fkeys\">\n     <div class=\"fkey act\">F1</div><div class=\"fkey\">F2</div><div class=\"fkey\">F3</div><div class=\"fkey\">F4</div><div class=\"fkey\">F5</div><div class=\"fkey\">F6</div><div class=\"fkey\">F7</div><div class=\"fkey\">F8</div><div class=\"fkey\">F9</div><div class=\"fkey\">F10</div><div class=\"fkey\">F11</div><div class=\"fkey off\">F12</div>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"plate\">Training Simulation &mdash; Not For Operational Use</div>\n </div>\n</div>",
    "design_notes": "From the screenshots I kept the console architecture: a heavy dark bezel around a phosphor-green screen, a status strip with the mode word at the top, a narrow left parameter rail, a sector scope drawn in CSS/SVG with range rings and a wedge, tabular side panels on the right, a full-width control strip along the bottom and an F1–F12 key row. From the profile I drove the substance: the air-picture slot is the dominant panel and is laid out for the eight readout fields in order (TRK, SPD, ALT, TYPE, ID, FIRE STATUS, TTI, PK), the identification key lists only Our Forces / Friendly / Unknown / Enemy with friendly-blue, friendly-green, neutral-amber and hostile-red tones, the rail shows the fixed 120° sector, operator-adjustable tilt, class detection ranges and the 70/50/20 km engagement bands, and the decision strip is sized for the full seven-step commit sequence plus tilt, with the two-rockets-in-the-air limit annotated. Deliberately omitted or generalised: all Hebrew titles, vendor/product wording, unit markings and numeric readouts from the screenshots; the trajectory-analysis and diagnostics/logistics pages were not reproduced as capabilities (no correlate-tracks or auto-function controls exist), and nothing implies an external release authority since the profile records none.",
